[[Maintenance therapy in classical follicular lymphoma]]

!! Design and findings

Standard 2-year rituximab maintenance was compared with a PET/MRD-adapted strategy after R-CHOP or BR. The experimental arm used observation for complete metabolic/MRD-negative responders, MRD-triggered rituximab for molecular positivity, and radioimmunotherapy followed by maintenance for incomplete metabolic response. Standard maintenance produced better PFS; the BR subgroup analysis also favored it.

!! Practical interpretation

This was a comparison with a mixed response-adapted strategy, not observation for all BR responders. It argues against describing the BR evidence as entirely absent or using PET/MRD negativity alone to omit maintenance routinely. [[FOLL12, Luminari et al., 2022|https://doi.org/10.1200/JCO.21.01234]] [[BR subgroup, Nizzoli et al., 2023|https://doi.org/10.1002/hon.3184]]

Evidence reviewed September 7, 2026.
